From ca204ff56f50dbaf3a5d01839a5e3e793bc5af73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:40:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a read-only Certificates page

Lists every certificate Caddy has under certificate_dir/certificates,
recursively, using the same data-table UI as Site Blocks and Logs
(search, page size, pagination -- no filters). Columns are CN,
Provider (Local vs Let's Encrypt/ZeroSSL/etc, read off the issuer
folder Caddy's certmagic storage layer already sorts certs into),
Expiry (green when healthy, red within 2 weeks of expiry or already
expired), and a disabled placeholder Actions button.

Parses each .crt's leaf PEM block with the `cryptography` library
(added to requirements.txt) rather than trusting the on-disk site-name
folder, so a hand-edited or renamed cert still reports its real CN.
Files that don't parse as a certificate are silently skipped, since
Caddy's storage directory can hold other bookkeeping (lock files,
metadata JSON) this page has no business about.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
